Serve attachments that keep their content in the database even when they have a url.

With ir_attachment.location set to db, asset bundles (url /web/assets/...) were answered
with a 301 redirect to their own url, so the web client loaded without styles or scripts.
Upstream: odoo/odoo issues #292774 and #293047, pull request #293193.

The Dockerfile applies this after checking out Odoo, and skips it when the checkout already
contains the change. Delete this file and that Dockerfile step once a 20.0 build contains the fix.

diff --git a/odoo/addons/base/models/ir_attachment.py b/odoo/addons/base/models/ir_attachment.py
index 88c4e073c1d..40682e97c91 100644
--- a/odoo/addons/base/models/ir_attachment.py
+++ b/odoo/addons/base/models/ir_attachment.py
@@ -1143,7 +1143,9 @@ class IrAttachment(models.Model):
             except OSError:
                 pass
 
-        elif self.url:
+        elif self.url and not self.db_datas:
+            # the url of an attachment with content in the database (e.g. an
+            # asset bundle) is its own address, not a redirection target
             return Stream(type='url', url=self.url, **kw)
 
         data = self.raw.content
